# A module name first bound to a NUMBER and rebound to a STRING (or a list,
# or any object) INSIDE A BLOCK was stored raw into the number's slot: this
# loop printed 6291688, the string's address, where CPython prints `sss`, and
# leaked the string every pass. Neither binding is a shape the module pre-pass
# can read inside a block, so nothing widened the slot to a variant. Until it
# can, the compiler refuses this by name, pointing at the annotation that
# makes it work (the sibling test_nilpy_a_module_name_annotated_any_*).
# bug-n-a-module-name-rebound-to-another-type-inside-a-block-stores-raw
a = [1, 2, 3]
for k in range(2):
    x = len(a)
    x = "s" * 3
    print(x)
